    "buoyancy": {
      "word": "BUOYANCY",
      "definitions": [
        {
          "text": "The property of floating on the surface of a liquid, or in a fluid, as in the atmosphere; specific lightness, which is inversely as the weight compared with that of an equal volume of water.",
          "partOfSpeech": "noun"
        },
        {
          "text": "(Physics)",
          "partOfSpeech": "noun"
        },
        {
          "text": "The upward pressure exerted upon a floating body by a fluid, which is equal to the weight of the body; hence, also, the weight of a floating body, as measured by the volume of fluid displaced. Such are buoyancies or displacements of the different classes of her majesty's ships. Eng. Cyc.",
          "partOfSpeech": "noun"
        },
        {
          "text": "Cheerfulness; vivacity; liveliness; sprightliness; -- the opposite of Ant: heaviness; as, buoyancy of spirits.",
          "partOfSpeech": "noun"
        }
      ],
